// ADR-009 C3 #14 slice 3 (S3c) — the EVALUATE-ONCE pin, single application
// (charter item (d)). The side-effecting comptime config expression is the
// `warning("cfg-eval")` call in the annotation handler: handler-run warnings
// surface on the subprocess STDERR as `warning[C0002]: cfg-eval` lines
// (probed S3c 2026-07-20 — `surface_comptime_warnings`, LSDS terminal
// render, `functions_annotations.rs` handler seam). The CLI cell counts the
// marker: EXACTLY ONE occurrence per application, in BOTH modes, while the
// woven target runs a 200-call hot loop crossing T1@100 — the capture value
// is comptime-evaluated ONCE at binding and BAKED as a constant; nothing
// re-evaluates at invocation time. CONTRAST (the S0 §4 a4e evidence, legacy
// path, byte-unchanged until S6): today's legacy config path re-evaluates
// the config expression PER INVOCATION (`[5] fired` … `[6] fired` after a
// module-binding mutation between calls).
//
// #65 FENCE: the config array literal is HOISTED to a handler local first —
// `[capture("cfg", [10, 20])]` inline would trip the PRE-EXISTING #65
// `pending_variable_typed_array_kind` leak. #65 is NOT fixed in S3.
//
// The annotation `comptime post` handler is NOT a top-level comptime block
// (parse-based vacuity guard).
//
// Value-distinguishing arithmetic, per call i in 0..200:
//   before: a0 = i + cfg[0] + cfg.length() = i + 12
//   impl:   * 10 → 10i + 120;  sum = 10*19900 + 120*200 = 223000
// Expected stdout: 223000  (skipped before → sum 10i = 199000)
fn tmpl<Args>(args: Args, cfg: Array<int>) -> Args {
  args[0] = args[0] + cfg[0] + cfg.length()
  return args
}

annotation hooked() on function {
  comptime post(target, ctx) {
    warning("cfg-eval")
    let cfg = [10, 20]
    install(before_hook(tmpl, [capture("cfg", cfg)]))
  }
}

@hooked()
fn calc(a: int) -> int { a * 10 }

fn run() -> int {
  let mut total = 0
  for i in 0..200 { total = total + calc(i) }
  total
}
print(run())
